  "interpretation": [
    "The showcase structure uses fillMm .17, stitchPitchMm .18, stitchRelief .85, stitchFan .65, stitchFlow .75, shortStitchGuard 1, netRelaxation 1.3 and netOrganic .65. R12 grouping 0 and R13 grouping .65 are reported separately; the prior core-default 36812-path count did not describe the showcase.",
    "The radial probe is linear direct-diffuse angular response on one elliptical yarn, before RGB conversion, tone mapping, inter-yarn shadowing or IBL. Its min/max are angular response extrema, not pixel brightness. It is not a rendered-image quality score or a complete BSDF-energy measurement.",
    "Each target diffuse distribution integrates to pi on the actual normal hemisphere and is zero outside it. The blend retains the old softness response at its remaining weight.",
    "The orientation field has no albedo modulation and no per-path seed, UV, time or camera-dependent noise. Pixel-footprint filtering affects each band.",
    "Original through scattering, cross-section/Fresnel factor, incident RGB/shadow paths, geometry/radius/alpha/hole coverage remain unchanged.",
    "This candidate can soften lit rod shading but cannot turn separate needle geometry into connected physical fibres. Motif grouping is an independent structural candidate.",
    "Main-thread matched whole-fabric and yarn renders, plus GPU timings, determine whether the visual benefit warrants enabling it. No visual-pass or measured-BSDF claim is made."
  ]
